ries, debug and release"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The same targets as macOS, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSetNoteTests"},{"type":"text","text":" (the note walk)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"CI’s Linux Bazel and SwiftPM jobs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"WebAssembly, a 32-bit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":", debug and release"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSetsTests"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSetsPerformanceTests"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"just wasi-test"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"just wasi-test -c release"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Windows, modules linked statically"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSetsTests"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSetsPerformanceTests"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSetPaddedSectionTests"},{"type":"text","text":" (the padding walk, on every platform)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"CI’s Windows workflow, when Windows code changes","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Android (aarch64, an Android 15 emulator), modules linked statically and a library loaded with ","type":"text"},{"code":"dlopen","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", debug and release","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"LinkerSetsTests","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"LinkerSetNoteTests","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" among them), ","type":"text"},{"code":"LinkerSetsPerformanceTests","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"LinkerSetsDynamicTests","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"dlopen","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"just android-test"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"just android-test -c release"},{"text":", on a Mac; not in CI","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Android, a shared library linked at launch","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Untested: the test of it builds under Bazel only; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dl_iterate_phdr"},{"type":"text","text":" reads it as it does a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dlopen"},{"type":"text","text":"ed library"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A WebAssembly program is one statically linked module, so it has no shared libraries to search."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Linking-modes","text":"Linking modes","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Records survive dead stripping (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-dead_strip"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"--gc-sections"},{"text":") in debug and release builds: each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record is marked ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@used"},{"text":", and the section is kept. Shared libraries carry their own records,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"found once the loader has mapped them, whether linked at launch or opened later with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dlopen"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record is in the program only if its object file is. SwiftPM and Bazel link every module a target","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"depends on. A build that pulls a static archive’s members in only on demand leaves out a module","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing calls into: link it whole with ","type":"text"},{"code":"-force_load","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (Apple platforms) or ","type":"text"},{"code":"--whole-archive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(Linux).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Loading-and-unloading-during-a-read","text":"Loading and unloading during a read","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A read takes a snapshot: every image loaded when the walk reaches it is read whole, and an image","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"loaded or unloaded while a read runs is either in that read’s records in full or absent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Format"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An image loaded during a read","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An image unloaded during a read"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mach-O"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Found if dyld added it before the walk took its lock, missed otherwise"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"dyld calls the remove callback before it unmaps an image, and the callback waits for the walk’s lock, so the image is read whole or not at all. dyld never unmaps an image that holds Swift code"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"ELF","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dl_iterate_phdr"},{"text":" holds the loader’s lock for the whole walk, so a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dlopen"},{"text":" finishing during it waits, and is missed","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"code":"dlclose","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" waits for the walk the same way","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"COFF","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Found if ","type":"text"},{"code":"K32EnumProcessModules","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" listed it, missed otherwise","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each module is pinned with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GetModuleHandleExW"},{"text":" while its headers are read; one freed before that is left out","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"WebAssembly","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A program is one module; nothing loads or unloads"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The next read sees the change: a library opened since is found, and one the loader has unmapped"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"since is gone."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Records-of-a-closed-library","text":"Records of a closed library","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record’s accessor and the value it hands back live in the record’s image, and so does the Swift","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"metadata of the record’s type. On Apple platforms dyld never unmaps an image that holds Swift code,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so a library with records stays mapped after ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dlclose"},{"text":": its records are still found, and they and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their values stay valid.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"On Linux and Android the loader unmaps a library once its last handle is closed, but the Swift","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"runtime keeps the library’s type metadata and conformances registered. After that, the process can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"crash in any later dynamic cast or ","type":"text"},{"code":"print","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whether or not LinkerSets reads anything. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSetRecord","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" copied out of the library also holds a dangling accessor,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSetRecord\/value(as:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" would call. LinkerSets can’t detect either","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"case, because nothing tells a copied record that its image is gone.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Don’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"dlclose","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" a library that holds Swift code, records included, while the process runs. Open","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plug-ins once and keep them open; a library opened with ","type":"text"},{"code":"RTLD_NODELETE","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" stays mapped after","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"dlclose","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Closing a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"library without Swift code (a C library) is safe while another thread reads: the walk never touches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an image that is going away.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking"},"references":{"doc://LinkerSetsRuntime/documentation/LinkerSetsRuntime/LinkerSetRecord":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsruntime\/linkersetrecord","type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSetRecord","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":